  "notes": "{喚|わめ}く implies loud, often uncontrolled shouting or screaming. It often has a negative connotation suggesting the person is being unreasonable or hysterical.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {叫|さけ}ぶ: to shout, to scream (more neutral)\n- {怒鳴|どな}る: to yell angrily (specifically angry)\n- {騒|さわ}ぐ: to make noise, to be rowdy (broader meaning)",
